  "answer": "Based on the BRFSS Prevalence & Trends Data (2011-present) from CDC, here are the states with prevalence below 45% of adults who had at least one drink of alcohol within the past 30 days, between 2019 and 2022:\n\n## States with prevalence below 45% in at least one year (2019-2022)\n\n**Alabama (AL):** 2019: 42.2%, 2020: 44.2%, 2021: 40.3%, 2022: 43.6%\n\n**Arkansas (AR):** 2019: 40.8%, 2020: 43.6%, 2021: 42.9%, 2022: 44.5%\n\n**Guam (GU):** 2019: 41.6%, 2020: 41.4%, 2021: 39.8%, 2022: 44.1%\n\n**Kentucky (KY):** 2019: 42.3%, 2021: 39.2%, 2022: 35.2% (2020 data: 45.1%)\n\n**Mississippi (MS):** 2019: 39.4%, 2020: 39.1%, 2021: 40.0%, 2022: 42.3%\n\n**Oklahoma (OK):** 2019: 42.0%, 2020: 40.3%, 2021: 41.4%, 2022: 43.5%\n\n**Puerto Rico (PR):** 2019: 31.6%, 2020: 31.2%, 2021: 32.7%, 2022: 34.6%\n\n**Tennessee (TN):** 2019: 44.8% (other years above 45%)\n\n**Utah (UT):** 2019: 31.1%, 2020: 30.9%, 2021: 32.6%, 2022: 33.8%\n\n**West Virginia (WV):** 2019: 37.4%, 2020: 36.6%, 2021: 37.0%, 2022: 39.7%\n\n---\n\n## States consistently below 45% across ALL available years 2019-2022\n\n**Alabama (AL):** 42.2%, 44.2%, 40.3%, 43.6%\n\n**Arkansas (AR):** 40.8%, 43.6%, 42.9%, 44.5%\n\n**Guam (GU):** 41.6%, 41.4%, 39.8%, 44.1%\n\n**Mississippi (MS):** 39.4%, 39.1%, 40.0%, 42.3%\n\n**Oklahoma (OK):** 42.0%, 40.3%, 41.4%, 43.5%\n\n**Puerto Rico (PR):** 31.6%, 31.2%, 32.7%, 34.6%\n\n**Utah (UT):** 31.1%, 30.9%, 32.6%, 33.8%\n\n**West Virginia (WV):** 37.4%, 36.6%, 37.0%, 39.7%\n\n*Note: Kentucky (45.1% in 2020) and Tennessee (only 2019 below 45%) were below 45% in some years but not consistently across all four years.*",
